# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What never reaches a container build of this repository.
#
# Written 25 September 2026, beside deploy/Dockerfile.
#
# THE FIRST BLOCK IS THE POINT OF THIS FILE. This repository's settings file
# holds live Slack tokens and a bus password. A Dockerfile that copies only the
# files it names would not pick one up today, but a build context that CANNOT
# carry it is a different and better guarantee: it survives the next person who
# adds a COPY line. The pattern matches the whole family, the way .gitignore
# does here, because a timestamped backup once rode along in a commit for want
# of exactly that.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example

# Credentials and keys of any kind.
*.creds
*.pem
*.key

# A machine's own working state: a virtual environment belongs to the machine
# that made it, and copying one into an image mixes two interpreters.
.venv/
venv/
.git/
.langgraph_api/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# COMPILED PYTHON, AT EVERY DEPTH — and the '**/' matters.
#
# A pattern here is matched the way Docker matches one, not the way .gitignore
# does: a bare '__pycache__/' matches ONE directory, at the top, and nothing
# below it. Written that way on 25 September 2026, and the first image built
# from it carried a developer's own compiled files all the way down src/ — and
# each one of those has the absolute path of the machine that compiled it
# baked into it, which in that first image meant this machine's home directory,
# in a PUBLIC image. Found by sweeping the built image rather than by reading
# the file.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
